// BloodHound output written to disk
//
// Fires when a file lands with SharpHound's output naming: a 14-digit timestamp, an
// underscore, then users, computers, groups or another data type as .json, the BloodHound
// zip, or the random names it uses with --randomfilenames. SharpHound's source adds the
// timestamp even when the names are random, so that's what the rule keys on. A renamed
// SharpHound still writes these.
//
// Runs:      Continuous (NRT)
// Severity:  High
// MITRE:     T1087.002, T1069.002, T1482
// Tables:    DeviceFileEvents
// Custom details: InitiatingProcessAccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName, FolderPath
//
// Needs:
//   - Nothing beyond Defender for Endpoint.
//
// Heads up: Defender limits how many file events it records. Run SharpHound once in a lab
// and check the .json and .zip files show up in DeviceFileEvents before you trust this one.
// A custom --zipfilename won't match, but the .json files it writes first still do.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check the folder, the process that wrote the file and the account.
//   - Escalate unless it's an approved pentest. Grab the zip if it's still there, it shows
//     what they collected.
//   - Close only for an approved test.
//
// Based on: SharpHound's source (BaseContext.cs, OutputWriter.cs), SharpHoundCommon's
// DataType list, Sigma "BloodHound Collection Files".

DeviceFileEvents
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1d)
| where ActionType in ("FileCreated", "FileCreatedAggregatedReport")
| where FileName matches regex @'(?i)(?:^|_)\d{14}_(?:users|groups|computers|domains|gpos|ous|containers|rootcas|aiacas|ntauthstores|enterprisecas|certtemplates|issuancepolicies|sites|siteservers|sitesubnets)\.json$|(?:^|_)\d{14}_bloodhound(?:loopresults)?\.zip$|(?:^|_)\d{14}_(?-i:[a-z0-9]{8}\.[a-z0-9]{3})$'
| project Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceId, DeviceName, FileName, FolderPath, SHA1, InitiatingProcessAccountDomain, InitiatingProcessAccountName, InitiatingProcessAccountSid, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine
